; ROTATE SIXTEEN  entered at the first byte of a sixteen byte run with one
; free cell immediately below it; every byte moves down one place and the
; first wraps round to the top; the pointer comes back where it started;
;
; THIS IS THE CONVEYOR  and it is how a loop reaches sixteen bytes without an
; index: turn the run instead of walking to it  and the byte under the fixed
; read point is a different one each turn; sixteen turns put the run back as
; it was;
;
; IT IS AFFORDABLE HERE AND NOWHERE NEAR A TABLE; one turn of sixteen cells
; measures 12 thousand 314 instructions on FIPS 197 Appendix B's round one
; state; In aes/subbytes the loop machinery  this turning plus the two
; seventeen cell byte moves that feed the walk  costs 324 thousand for a pass
; of sixteen against the 4 million 750 thousand of the walks it enables: six
; point eight percent;
;
; THE FILE CAME OUT SIX POINT FOUR PERCENT DEARER AND NOT SIX POINT EIGHT
; and the gap between those two numbers is the whole reason this paragraph
; names both; the looped cut of aes/subbytes also swapped a PACKED ABSOLUTE
; table for block/sbox256's delta coded one  which is 17 thousand
; instructions cheaper on its own  so the net against the unrolled file is
; 307 thousand where the loop machinery alone is 324 thousand; Quoting the
; net as the cost of the turning would credit the conveyor with a saving that
; belongs to the table;
;
; THAT SHARE IS NOT A CONSTANT AND THIS COMMENT WOULD LIE IF IT SAID SO; a
; turn's cost tracks the byte values it carries  79 instructions on a run
; of nought  and 29 thousand 404 on a run of 0xff  while a walk's tracks
; the index it walks to; So the share runs from four point one percent on a
; state of 0xff to worse than double on a state of nought  where every walk
; stops at the first group and there is nothing for the turning to amortise;
; The figure above is quoted at a published state because real states are
; not nought;
;
; One turn of a 256 cell table costs about as much as a whole walk  which is
; why the table is walked and only the state is turned; HANDOFF carries the
; measurements;
; the first byte drops into the free cell below the run
  [-<+>]
; and every other byte moves down one place
  >[-<+>]>[-<+>]>[-<+>]>[-<+>]>[-<+>]>[-<+>]>[-<+>]>[-<+>]
  >[-<+>]>[-<+>]>[-<+>]>[-<+>]>[-<+>]>[-<+>]>[-<+>]
; the pointer is on the last byte now  and the one that dropped out comes
; back round to fill it
  L16
  [-R16+L16]
  R16
; and home to the first byte
  L15
